# Milestone: M3
# Covers: onleave handler runs when the tagged block is terminated by
#         tag.stop(); the onleave body executes before the stop propagates.
#
# defer-to: T29
#
# Reason: same as onleave_normal_exit.chk — requires both UTag runtime (T29)
# and `onleave` parse/emit (M5 or whichever milestone lands it first).  The
# C-level plumbing (TAG_SCOPE + FLAG_HAS_ONLEAVE + run_cleanup_with_replace)
# is in place at M3 (T11); only the parse/emit path and the UTag runtime are
# missing.
#
# When both land, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: onleave runs ("cleanup") when tag is stopped externally.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29 / M5):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var cleaned = 0;
#   t: { t.stop() } onleave { cleaned = 1 };
#   cleaned
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 1
